{"content":[{"c":["RATHAMIN*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["A territory transferred from the dominion of Samaria to Judah by Demetrius of Syria. A letter from Demetrius to his adjutant Lasthenes authorizing the transfer is mentioned in ",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.11.34","r":"1Macc.11.34","rawR":"1Macc.11.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.11.34","value":"1Macc.11.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Maccabees 11:34"},". The word is sometimes translated Ramathaim (",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"), the birthplace of Samuel and home of Elkanah and Hannah (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.1.1,19","r":"1Sam.1.1,19","rawR":"1Sam.1.1,19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.1.1,19","value":"1Sam.1.1,19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 1:1, 19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.2.19","r":"1Sam.2.19","rawR":"1Sam.2.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.2.19","value":"1Sam.2.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:19"},"). In that case, it figures prominently in OT history, for there Saul first made acquaintance with Samuel (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.9.6,10","r":"1Sam.9.6,10","rawR":"1Sam.9.6,10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.9.6,10","value":"1Sam.9.6,10"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:6, 10"},"), there Samuel retreated after his last break with Saul, and there Samuel’s grave is located (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.25.1","r":"1Sam.25.1","rawR":"1Sam.25.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.25.1","value":"1Sam.25.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:1"},"). Textual variants Armathaim (",{"c":["tev"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “Arimathea”) and Ramatha are partly explained by the transposition of ",{"c":["m"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," and ",{"c":["th"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," in the Septuagint version. Two modern sites are recommended for the ancient district: Beit Rime, 13 miles (20.9 kilometers) east and north of Lydda, and Ramallah, 8 miles (12.9 kilometers) north of Jerusalem."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Rathamin","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Maccabees 11:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Macc.11.34","rawQueryValue":"1Macc.11.34","sourceRefExact":"1Macc.11.34"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 1:1, 19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.1.1,19","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.1.1,19","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.1.1,19"},{"anchorText":"2:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.2.19","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.2.19","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.2.19"},{"anchorText":"9:6, 10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.9.6,10","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.9.6,10","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.9.6,10"},{"anchorText":"25:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.25.1","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.25.1","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.25.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"1f0984e03429243ba5433b6db03e89392b66620bf1ade521b8e57ac94704c97e","sourceItemName":"Rathamin","sourceItemOrder":63,"sourceMember":"Articles/R.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rathamin","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Rathamin*","title":"Rathamin*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}